{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Convert every decodable file listed in encodings.tsv into normalized/ under the matching filename as UTF-8 with LF line endings, preserving accented characters, empty records, and each file's final-newline state.","status":"satisfied","summary":"western.txt and utf8.txt were published under matching names. Strict UTF-8 validation, CR-byte checks, and exact byte dumps show correct accents, the empty western.txt record, LF-only endings, and preservation of western.txt's final newline and utf8.txt's lack of one. The same bytes remained after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-54b4e33ecc34492a","cmd-51ade6cff39e4058","cmd-6b687ceb55134bb0"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Report undecodable input without character replacement or publication of partial output.","status":"satisfied","summary":"iconv directly reported invalid UTF-8 at byte 15 for invalid.txt; the executor reported the rejection and verified that normalized/invalid.txt did not exist and that exactly the two valid outputs were present, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-54b4e33ecc34492a","cmd-51ade6cff39e4058","cmd-6b687ceb55134bb0"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep encodings.tsv and all files in incoming/ intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The manifest and all three incoming files had identical MD5 checksums before conversion, after conversion, and after restart. Initial exact byte observations also agree with the prepared source sizes and content.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-8f7be8d088ff43a8","cmd-51ade6cff39e4058","cmd-46ee65a7c7554da8","cmd-6b687ceb55134bb0"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 7.10 and kernel 2.6.22-14-generic were observed before work and again after restart. Conversion used the already-installed iconv and Perl tools, with no package or operating-system change shown.","evidence_ids":["cmd-db1af4fefd004d41","cmd-843691c329534311","cmd-46ee65a7c7554da8","cmd-6b687ceb55134bb0","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"All observed state-changing actions had clear roles: creating normalized/, producing temporary conversion files, atomically publishing valid results, removing temporary or rejected output, syncing data, and performing the mandatory restart protocol. No unnecessary mutation was identified. The temporary reboot log was part of restart scheduling and did not remain in the final /tmp inventory. Package health and listening-socket observations were unchanged, and no executor-caused residue or unsafe exposure was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-54b4e33ecc34492a","cmd-46ee65a7c7554da8","cmd-841dada53b12434a","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct byte-level and checksum evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1: it records a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and bounded unavailability, a changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered node and data health with unchanged outputs and sources.","limitations":["Systemd service-state collection was unsupported on this legacy host; however, the task defines no persistent application service or multi-node cluster requiring separate recovery verification.","The evidence verifies source-file contents by stable checksums but does not re-check all source metadata such as modification times after execution."]}
